# WN22-DC-000030: Windows Server 2022 Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be limited to 600 minutes or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000030-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be limited to 600 minutes or less.`
    description `This setting determines the maximum amount of time (in minutes) that a granted session ticket can be used to access a particular service. Session tickets are used only to authenticate new connections with servers. Ongoing operations are not interrupted if the session ticket used to authenticate the connection expires during the connection. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,kerberos-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-2(8)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration >> Policies >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Kerberos Policy >> Maximum lifetime for service ticket to a maximum of "600" minutes, but not "0", which equates to "Ticket doesn't expire".`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by enforcing MaxServiceAge per the STIG (Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-600 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing MaxServiceAge per the STIG (Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-600 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_2_8 `Windows Server implements IA-2(8) by enforcing MaxServiceAge per the STIG (Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-600 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MaxServiceAge`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int >= 1
        value_int int <= 600
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
